WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.900
After loaning Spider-Man out to join the Avengers
at Marvel Studios, Sony is eager to get its

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.660
own adjacent Marvel universe back on track
with the other characters in its stable — and

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.639
Tom Hardy is hoping to start things off right
with Venom.

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:16.770
Making a Spider-Man movie that doesn't really
focus on the wall-crawler is a tall order,

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.340
but it looks like Sony's found the right man
for the job.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.750
Here's why Tom Hardy will blow everyone away
as Venom when the movie hits theaters in October

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.950
2018.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.640
Familiar territory

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.950
Hardy doesn't just bring name recognition
to Venom; he also brings the chops.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.980
When the stars finally aligned for director
George Miller to get Mad Max: Fury Road off

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.620
the ground, he tapped Hardy to follow Mel
Gibson in bringing Max to life.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.030
It was a tall order, but Hardy did a perfect
job of capturing the quiet, action-packed

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.510
intensity that made Max such a fan favorite
character.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:51.320
The movie also featured some of the most ridiculously
insane stunts ever attempted, so whatever

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.000
Sony cooks up for Venom, Hardy should be prepared.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.890
Plus, when you think of Hardy's résumé,
his role as Bane in Christopher Nolan's The

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.170
Dark Knight Rises is likely one of the first
to come to mind.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.710
Hardy joined the final installment in Nolan's
Batman trilogy to play the classic DC baddie,

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:10.390
one of the most physical and menacing roles
in comic movie history—a character who pushed

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.530
the Dark Knight further than he's ever been
pushed, and almost beat him in the end.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:17.470
"Why didn't you kill me?"

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.420
"You don't fear death.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.170
You welcome it.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.690
Your punishment must be more severe."

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.890
We don't know exactly which direction they'll
be taking this version of Venom, but it stands

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.841
to reason he'll be somewhere between villain
and anti-hero — so Hardy's experience as

00:01:32.841 --> 00:01:35.799
a straight-up comics baddie should come in
handy.

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:37.210
Much-needed range

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.580
Fans had mixed reactions to the first Venom
teaser, mostly because it didn't really show

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.850
all that much Venom.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:47.550
Instead, the film is being framed as a psychological
thriller dealing with the fallout of mind-melding

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:48.570
with a symbiote.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.369
It's an aspect of the story that's certainly
been explored in the comics, but rarely on

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:54.830
the big screen with any real depth.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:58.540
Outside of his two biggest genre roles, Hardy
has a varied career that should serve him

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.060
well with whatever curveballs playing the
character might call for.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.260
Hardy's had roles in everything from Sucker
Punch to Inception, and took on period parts

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.799
in films like The Revenant.

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:10.940
He's even gone the romantic comedy route in
This Means War.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.099
More recently, he's been spreading his wings
on the small screen in critical hits like

00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:19.430
Peaky Blinders, and he reunited with Christopher
Nolan for the acclaimed writer-director's

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.489
hit World War II drama Dunkirk.

00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:24.280
Clearly, Hardy's ready for pretty much anything.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.480
Spot-on look

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.430
The first Venom teaser trailer gave us a look
at Hardy's version of Eddie Brock, and at

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.670
least from an aesthetic standpoint, he seems
to have nailed it.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.700
Hardy's rough and tumble vibe and muscular
frame are a perfect match for the comics'

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.080
take on the character.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.280
Anytime an actor signs on for a superhero
movie, it's typically assumed they'll spend

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.860
a decent bit of time behind a mask.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.860
Hardy pretty much never got out from behind
his Bane mask in The Dark Knight Rises, but

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.440
that doesn't look to be a concern in Venom.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.610
All the teaser footage showed Hardy playing
Brock outside the Venom suit, and though we'll

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.569
certainly see the suit in the full film, it
looks like Hardy will have ample opportunity

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:02.690
to shine as the Brock we know from the comics
when he isn't behind that toothy symbiote

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:03.690
face.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:07.590
Also working in Hardy's favor: the only other
live-action version of Eddie Brock we've ever

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:12.379
seen came courtesy of That '70s Show vet Topher
Grace in Spider-Man 3.

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:16.420
Nothing against Grace, but it'd be difficult
for Hardy not to be an improvement.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.430
Thanks for watching!

